SDK patch 0320 (Max Payne 3 port), v7: x360_edram_8bits_a_flotante, DEFAULT FALSE. The tonemap's
finished 8-bit picture is snapshotted BY THE COPY ENGINE right after the tonemap's own draw - without
touching the running pass - and the frontal copy installs it into the 7e3 view it is about to resolve,
as values. Root cause it closes (PORTING.md, runs 23-35 item 3 and the carry saga): the tonemap draws
the picture into base 198's f0 view; the frame's later 8-bit writers of the SAME pass bury it before
the pass closes; the final copy reads the f12 view of those tiles, which keeps the raw lit scene.

The model (v1-v6, console evidence; PORTING.md "The carry saga, v7"):
- The tonemap's own 8-bit output IS the picture (v1: colored exactly when the tonemap was the last
  8-bit writer before the final copy).
- The tonemap, the no-VS probes and the composite (vs 573 ps 1895) share ONE renderer pass (identical
  claves - base, format, pitch, MSAA); the probes are rejected before the claves check (dibujos.cpp,
  the VS lookup at ~567 precedes the pass-change test at ~1840), so the pass closes only at the f0
  resolve, AFTER the composite. v4's close-only snapshot therefore installed the composite's output:
  black gameplay at 1.0 install/frame.
- The composite is NOT fed by 0654D000 (that was puzzle (ii)'s guess): its only sampler is the DEPTH
  resolve 0820A000 fmt 23 (mp3_030 draw 2310). It is the game's own stencil-directed effect layer,
  rendered wrong in the port - a separate defect; v7 sidesteps it by snapshotting BEFORE it.
- Puzzle (i) dissolves: the resolve machinery reads the f0 image's own pixels correctly (v1's carries
  prove the swap/3D-copy source). The "f0 colored / 0654D000 black" disagreement compared different
  frames: 0654D000 is resolved twice a frame (the G-buffer c2 at base 288 first, then the tonemap's
  f0), and in composite frames its black content is the composite's doing, not a resolve-source bug.
- v6's fully-black console run (its log was never read, so the draw cannot be named offline): the
  after-draw snapshot re-armed its own gate (every snapshot invalidated the pass, and the re-begin set
  edram_pase_post_ again from the next post draw), so the installed content became "whatever the LAST
  post draw anywhere wrote into any same-sized 8-bit target" - the install is keyed by dimensions
  only - plus mid-pass target-rebinding surgery on shared paths the close never touched. v7 keeps the
  moment but not the machinery.

v7's design (the smallest footprint the model supports):
- THE SNAPSHOT: dibujos.cpp, right after the FIRST post draw (the tonemap quad) of a post-begun pass
  into an RGBA8 target, one per pass (edram_pase_post_ is consumed on success; the pass's later post
  draws and the shared close cannot overwrite it). The copy is dkCmdBufCopyImage - the copy engine
  binds no render targets, sets no state, invalidates nothing: the pass and its recorded state (g_)
  survive, NO re-begin (v6 rebound and re-began the pass around every post draw and blackened even the
  cutscenes v4 had colored). No source preparation either: at that moment the target holds exactly
  what the draw wrote (v6's RestaurarContenido/HacerBorradoPendiente/CompletarBanda here could clear
  its rows mid-pass). Two barriers order the copy against the draw before it and the draws after it.
- THE CLOSE FALLBACK IS GONE (EdramCerrarPase): the tonemap's pass closes at the resolve, after the
  composite - a close snapshot can only install a later writer's output (v4's black gameplay). The
  end-of-close edram_pase_post_ reset stays (v5 dropped it and the gate leaked stale-true).
- THE INSTALL (destinos.cpp Copiar, v4's proven firing): at a frontal resolve of a format-3 view,
  Copiar3D carries the side image (RGBA8) into the 7e3 view as VALUES (RGBA8 -> RGBA16F, v1's proven
  direction), right before the copy reads it. New in v7: only a snapshot of THIS frame installs
  (edram_posteado_fotograma_) - a stale side image must not paint a menu after gameplay.
- MENUS AND CUTSCENES ARE UNTOUCHEN BY CONSTRUCTION: menus have no 8-bit post draw at all (v4.log's
  menu windows counted 0.0 installs and rendered colored by the default path); cutscenes snapshot
  their own tonemap draw - the same content v4's close snapshot installed there, colored - and the
  install happens after their whole post chain, at the frontal copy (v2's "later passes undo it"
  cannot reach it). Failure is safe: a snapshot that cannot be taken leaves edram_posteado_valido_
  false and the frame presents exactly as with the cvar off.

Off by default: this is architecture-level and must not change behavior until the console test enables
it via mp3.toml (x360_edram_8bits_a_flotante = true).

One console run decides:
- "[edram] snapshot post c 198 f0 960 #N (960x540 de 960x960) tras el dibujo, version V: ..." in a
  gameplay window + the 300-frame line at ~1.0 "de 8 bits a flotante" + colored gameplay: done.
- "[edram] snapshot post ... no tomado tras el dibujo, <razon>" names a death v5 could not.
- No snapshot line at all + 0.0 installs + the raw-white picture: the gate never engaged (the
  huella/pass-flag wiring - the [exposicion] tonemap line says which side).
- Snapshot line + sane probe values + 0.0 installs: the install's own conditions (frontal/formato/
  dims/frame) are the frontier.
- Snapshot line + "post fuente" probes at zero: the tonemap's own draw wrote nothing (the shader
  defect chain, [verts-tonemap]/[ubo-tonemap]) - not this patch's.

